# React Native (Expo) — Smart AC

Full detail: `.cursor/skills/code-standards-react/SKILL.md`.

## Layout (`apps/mobile/src`)

```text
components/
  base/          # reusable UI (buttons, cards)
  screens/       # full screens
  navigation/    # React Navigation (no Expo Router in MVP)
hooks/
stores/          # Zustand
theme/           # tokens + StyleSheet helpers
config/          # env (API URL, secret) — never commit secrets
```

## Components

- Functional only; props typed on parameters — **no `React.FC`**.
- Named exports; kebab-case files; PascalCase names.
- Split when useful: `foo.tsx`, `foo.styles.ts`, `foo.types.ts`.
- Props callbacks: `onPress`, `onChangeTemperature`. Parent: `handlePress`.
- Optional callbacks: `onPress?.()`.
- Keep components small; extract hooks for reusable logic.
- Prefer descriptive `const` over nested ternaries in JSX.

## Styling

- Styles live in `*.styles.ts` — no large inline style objects.
- Use theme tokens from `src/theme` (colors, spacing, radius, typography).
- Avoid magic numbers; name constants when needed.
- Lists: `FlatList` with stable `keyExtractor` — no index keys for dynamic data.

## State

- **Zustand** for shared device/API state (`stores/`).
- Local `useState` for ephemeral UI only.
- Separate UI flags (`isSubmitting`) from domain (`devices`).
- Named export for stores: `export const useDevicesStore = create(...)`.

## Navigation

- React Navigation stack — **not** Expo Router (MVP).
- Screen names via a typed const/enum — no raw string literals for routes.
- Type params with `NativeStackScreenProps` / `RouteProp`.

## Data

- No `fetch` in components — only `@smart-ac/api-client`.
- Types from `@smart-ac/shared`.
- Copy: “última orden / estado deseado”, never “el aire está en X” without `reportedState`.

## Testing

- Co-locate `*.test.ts(x)`; names without “should”.
- `renderElement` + `query` object pattern.
- Prefer RTL `screen` / user-event patterns; no `.only` in commits.

## Entry exception

`App.tsx` may use `export default` if Expo requires it; everything under `src/` uses named exports.
